  "summary": "Research run v2026-10-30-n284 (pending approval AR-20261030-03)\n\n- Panel: 284 firm-years across 32 listed housebuilders screened for residential revenue ≥50% (1840 土屋ホールディングス passes at 100%).\n- M1 P/B equation (n=284, scale 0.358): log P/B = 6.40×3yr ROE −0.30×growth +0.023×log revenue. M1 EV/EBITDA (n=241, scale 0.464): EV/EBITDA = −3.80×3yr margin +0.46×growth −0.059×log revenue.\n- Tsuchiya fitted multiples (2026 year effect): P/B 0.48 (0.31–0.77); EV/EBITDA 13.6 (7.5–24.7). Features: ROE 0.97%, growth −3.2%, margin 0.4%.\n- Annual backtest (9 non-overlapping years, 2016–2025): three methods clear the acceptance rule (mean IC>0, t≥2) — M1 EV/EBITDA (t=3.85), M1 P/B (t=2.48), P/E peers trailing (t=2.64). Four methods fail: P/B own history (t=0.71), P/B peers (t=0.67), EV/EBITDA own history (t=−0.23), EV/EBITDA peers (t=1.77).\n- Proposed weights blend equal share and accepted-method IC share: M1 EV/EBITDA 26.6%, P/E 22.7%, M1 P/B 22.2%, each other method 7.1%.\n- Weaknesses: only 32 companies; missing prices create survivorship bias; 4 of 7 methods not accepted by the backtest; live P/E and EV/EBITDA use forward estimates while their backtest uses trailing figures (no point-in-time forecast history).\n\n(Code check: 2 number(s) not found in the results and not verified: 20261030, 1840)",
